(** KQRChain.v -- long straight-line read-then-write bodies through the verified compiler (Rocq-C-solution.md F46, D28).

    Each step reads the memory and then writes it, so every memory of the text is used twice.  Checking that such a
    function equals the meaning of its syntax tree is exponential in the number of steps for Rocq's stock kernel (20 steps
    about 1 s, 30 steps over 120 s); our fork's kernel remembers, within one check, pairs of subterms already found equal
    (rocq-fork/), and checks them in milliseconds.  This file needs that kernel: the route's image is the fork
    (images.sh).  The per-program step is [exact_no_check]: the kernel checks it at [Qed], where the memo works. *)

